  "name": "Screen and rank CVs with Gmail, OpenAI, Airtable and Slack",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d4c8067a-5d46-495d-9d3b-bc4dc0d95bac",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        192,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## CV Screening & Ranking Pipeline\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow screens incoming job applications by extracting CV text, parsing the candidate profile with an LLM, combining it with a configured job description, and generating a candidate score and recommendation. It stores the ranked candidate in Airtable, then routes the application to Slack, Gmail, or a hold step depending on the recommendation. A separate scheduled branch creates a weekly hiring pipeline digest from Airtable and posts it to Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Gmail credentials for the application trigger and candidate booking email node.\n- Connect Google Drive credentials if the alternate Drive-based application trigger will be used.\n- Configure Airtable credentials, base IDs, table names, and fields for the job description config, candidate pipeline records, and weekly digest query.\n- Connect OpenAI credentials and verify the prompts/models used for CV parsing and candidate scoring.\n- Connect Slack credentials and set the channels for shortlist alerts, manual review posts, and weekly digest messages.\n- Confirm the file extraction nodes support the expected CV attachment formats, especially PDF and DOCX.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Airtable job description criteria, LLM prompts, scoring thresholds, and switch routing rules to match the hiring process and role-specific requirements."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5bfc9e9b-950f-4d4a-b08e-ebfffc795504",
